                                    <h2>FAQs</h2>
<h3>How much does a performance marketing agency cost in India in 2026?</h3>
<p>Retainers: <strong>&#8377;1.5L&ndash;&#8377;3L/month for growth</strong>, &#8377;3L&ndash;&#8377;6L for scale, &#8377;40K&ndash;&#8377;2L for single-channel. Ad spend is additional and paid directly to platforms.</p>
<h3>What ROAS should I expect from a performance marketing agency?</h3>
<p>Depends on category. <strong>Jewellery + electronics + home</strong>: 4&times;&ndash;7&times; blended. <strong>F&amp;B + skincare</strong>: 3&times;&ndash;5&times;. <strong>Fashion + beauty</strong>: 2.5&times;&ndash;4&times;. Anyone promising 10&times;+ is gaming metrics.</p>
<h3>Should I pay % of ad spend or fixed retainer?</h3>
<p><strong>Fixed retainer always.</strong> % of ad spend creates wrong incentive &mdash; agency wants more spend, not better ROAS.</p>
<h3>When is in-house cheaper than an agency?</h3>
<p><strong>Below &#8377;5L/month ad spend</strong>, in-house wins. <strong>Above &#8377;25L/month</strong>, hybrid beats pure-agency. Sweet spot for agency-only: &#8377;5L&ndash;&#8377;25L ad spend.</p>
<h3>How do you handle iOS 14.5+ attribution gap?</h3>
<p>Server-side CAPI + GTM SS + Enhanced Conversions + Aggregated Event Measurement + Stape / Stape-like server-side hosting. Real attribution recovered to ~75&ndash;90% of pre-ATT levels.</p>
<h3>Do you handle Amazon DSP + Quick Commerce ads?</h3>
<p>Yes &mdash; Amazon DSP + Sponsored Brands for electronics + general retail; Quick Commerce (Blinkit / Zepto / Instamart) for F&amp;B + grocery + personal care. Full marketplace + own-site + paid coordination.</p>
<h3>How quickly will I see results?</h3>
<p><strong>First qualified leads in 1&ndash;2 weeks</strong>; <strong>optimised ROAS in 4&ndash;6 weeks</strong>; <strong>dialled-in unit economics by month 3</strong>. Anyone promising sub-week results is gaming attribution.</p>


